From 77fdee3e951118d4120f0574437740df8d57ac28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:28:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/76] doc/examples/transcode: do not crash when the input
 cannot be opened

If avformat_open_input() fails, ifmt_ctx is NULL and stream_ctx has not
been allocated yet, but the cleanup code at the end of main() loops over
ifmt_ctx->nb_streams and indexes stream_ctx unconditionally. A missing
or unreadable input file therefore ends in a segmentation fault instead
of the error message:

  $ doc/examples/transcode nonexistent.mp4 out.mp4
  Cannot open input file
  Segmentation fault

The same happens when avformat_find_stream_info() fails, which returns
before stream_ctx is allocated.

Skip the loop when there is nothing to free. The example now prints
"Error occurred: No such file or directory" and returns 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/transcode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/transcode.c b/doc/examples/transcode.c
index 76afb32..e0e158c 100644
--- a/doc/examples/transcode.c
+++ b/doc/examples/transcode.c
@@ -676,7 +676,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     av_write_trailer(ofmt_ctx);
 end:
     av_packet_free(&packet);
-    for (i = 0; i < ifmt_ctx->nb_streams; i++) {
+    for (i = 0; ifmt_ctx && stream_ctx && i < ifmt_ctx->nb_streams; i++) {
         avcodec_free_context(&stream_ctx[i].dec_ctx);
         if (ofmt_ctx && ofmt_ctx->nb_streams > i && ofmt_ctx->streams[i] && stream_ctx[i].enc_ctx)
             avcodec_free_context(&stream_ctx[i].enc_ctx);
